{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/session-59128218.md", "content": "# Session note: wrapped-row tail recoloring (confirmed)

A confirmed recurring pattern uses a marker color on a background grid and output color 1. Inspect adjacent rows as wrapped runs: a run near the right edge of one row continues at column 0 of the next. When the selected wrapped motif's foreground run counts do not cover the full row width, recolor only the background cells strictly to the right of the upper row's run to 1; preserve the markers and the lower row. If the wrapped runs together cover the width, leave them unchanged. In the 18x9 demo, several adjacent row pairs had run lengths summing to 9 and stayed unchanged; the final pair had lengths 2 and 2, so only upper-row columns 4-8 became 1. The 29x11 test was solved correctly by applying the same operation to its first row: preserve its 8 at column 2, recolor columns 3-10 to 1, and leave all other cells unchanged.

